<div id="agno-diagram-explorer" class="de">
 <header class="de-top">
  <div class="de-identity"><a href="/en/labs/agno-architecture-v2/" aria-label="Back to architecture atlas">← Atlas</a><strong>AgentOS / Architecture diagrams</strong><span>SOURCE-VERIFIED</span></div>
  <div class="de-actions">
   <button type="button" id="de-only" aria-pressed="false"><span>▣</span> Diagram only</button>
   <button type="button" id="de-full" aria-pressed="false"><span>⛶</span> Fullscreen</button>
  </div>
 </header>
 <nav class="de-nav" aria-label="Choose architecture diagram" role="tablist">
  {panels.map((p,i)=><button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected={i===0} aria-controls={'de-scene-'+p.id} id={'de-tab-'+p.id} tabindex={i===0?0:-1} data-diagram={p.id}><span>{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><strong>{p.label}</strong><small>{p.subtitle}</small></button>)}
 </nav>
 <div class="de-heading"><div><span id="de-heading-label">01 / SYSTEM BOUNDARIES</span><h1 id="de-heading-title">What is actually deployed?</h1><p id="de-summary">AgentOS is a configurable FastAPI application. Providers and storage are dependencies, not built-in microservices.</p></div><a href={'https://github.com/agno-agi/agno/tree/'+revision} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pinned source {revision.slice(0,8)} ↗</a></div>
 <div class="de-body">
  <div class="de-stage" id="de-stage" tabindex="0" aria-label="Architecture diagram; drag to pan, scroll to zoom, and select components">
   {panels.map((p,i)=><div class="de-scene" role="tabpanel" id={'de-scene-'+p.id} aria-labelledby={'de-tab-'+p.id} data-scene={p.id} hidden={i!==0}>
     <svg class="de-svg" viewBox="0 0 1300 650" role="group" aria-label={p.label+' interactive source-linked diagram'} preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet">
      <defs>
       <pattern id={'de-grid-'+p.id} width="24" height="24" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><circle cx="1" cy="1" r="1" class="de-grid-point"/></pattern>
       {['http','call','event','data'].map(k=><marker id={'de-arrow-'+p.id+'-'+k} markerWidth="9" markerHeight="9" refX="8" refY="4.5" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L9 4.5 L0 9 Z" class={'de-head-'+k}/></marker>)}
      </defs>
      <rect width="1300" height="650" class="de-bg"/>
      <rect width="1300" height="650" fill={'url(#de-grid-'+p.id+')'}/>
      {p.regions.map(g=><g class={'de-region de-region-'+g.kind}><rect x={g.x} y={g.y} width={g.w} height={g.h} rx="18"/><text x={g.x+15} y={g.y+28}>{g.title}</text></g>)}
      {p.edges.map((e,i)=><g class={'de-edge de-edge-'+e[3]} data-edge={e[0]+'-'+e[1]} data-from={e[0]} data-to={e[1]} data-type={e[3]}><path d={connection(p,e)} marker-end={'url(#de-arrow-'+p.id+'-'+e[3]+')'}/><text x={edgeCaption(p,e).x} y={edgeCaption(p,e).y} class="de-edge-label">{e[2]}</text><title>{e[0]+' → '+e[1]+': '+e[2]}</title></g>)}
      {p.nodes.map(n=><g class={'de-node de-node-'+n.kind} role="button" tabindex="0" data-node={n.id} data-title={n.title} data-detail={n.explain} data-source={n.source} data-kind={n.kind} aria-label={'Inspect '+n.title}>
       <rect x={n.x} y={n.y} width={n.w} height={n.h} rx="11" class="de-node-rect"/>
       <rect x={n.x+9} y={n.y+13} width="5" height={n.h-26} rx="3" class="de-node-stripe"/>
       <text x={n.x+24} y={n.y+37} class="de-node-title">{n.title}</text>
       <text x={n.x+24} y={n.y+59} class="de-node-sub">{n.subtitle}</text>
      </g>)}
      <text x="30" y="626" class="de-footnote">* Optional / configuration dependent. Arrows are logical relationships, not recorded network traffic.</text>
     </svg>
     <div class="de-mobile-flow" aria-label={p.label+' as a readable vertical relationship map'}>
      {p.nodes.map((n,i)=><section class="de-mobile-card" data-mobile-card={n.id}>
       <button type="button" data-mobile-node={n.id} aria-label={'Inspect '+n.title}>
        <span>{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')} · {n.kind.toUpperCase()}</span><strong>{n.title}</strong><small>{n.subtitle}</small>
       </button>
       <p>{n.explain}</p>
       <div class="de-mobile-connections">
        {p.edges.filter(e=>e[0]===n.id).map(e=><span>→ <b>{lookup[p.id+':'+e[1]]?.title}</b><small>{e[2]}</small></span>)}
       </div>
       <a href={sourceBase+n.source} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read implementation ↗</a>
      </section>)}
     </div>
    </div>)}
   <div class="de-mobile-switch"><span>Readable component map</span><button type="button" id="de-mobile-canvas" aria-pressed="false">View diagram canvas →</button></div>
   <div class="de-canvas-controls" role="group" aria-label="Navigate diagram">
    <button id="de-zoom-in" type="button" aria-label="Zoom in">+</button>
    <button id="de-zoom-out" type="button" aria-label="Zoom out">−</button>
    <button id="de-fit" type="button">Fit</button>
   </div>
   <div class="de-legend"><span><i class="de-http"></i>HTTP</span><span><i class="de-call"></i>Python / lifecycle</span><span><i class="de-data"></i>Storage</span><span><i class="de-event"></i>Events</span></div>
  </div>
  <aside class="de-inspector" id="de-inspector" aria-live="polite">
   <span>SELECTED COMPONENT</span>
   <h2 id="de-inspect-title">Select a node</h2>
   <p id="de-inspect-detail">Choose a component in the diagram to see what it does, how it connects, and where its implementation lives.</p>
   <div class="de-source"><strong>SOURCE FILE</strong><a id="de-inspect-source" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href={'https://github.com/agno-agi/agno/tree/'+revision}>Browse pinned source ↗</a></div>
   <div class="de-relations"><strong>CONNECTED RELATIONSHIPS</strong><div id="de-relationships"><p>Click a node to reveal connected components and direction.</p></div></div><p class="de-inspect-meta" id="de-inspect-meta">Diagram components are grouped by ownership and deployment boundary.</p>
  </aside>
 </div>
 <footer class="de-lower">
  <div class="de-explain"><strong>How to read these diagrams</strong><p>Start with <b>How it is built</b>: create an Agent, provide it to AgentOS, call <code>get_app()</code> to build routes and startup lifespans, and serve the resulting ASGI application. Then follow <b>Inline request</b> to see <code>agent.arun()</code> and SSE; <b>Durable run</b> shows the optional database-backed queue and worker.</p></div>
  <div class="de-example"><span>MINIMAL ASSEMBLY · ILLUSTRATIVE</span><pre><code>agent = Agent(model=..., tools=[...])
os = AgentOS(agents=[agent], db=db)
app = os.get_app()
os.serve(app="app:app")</code></pre><small>Queue, Redis, tracing and MCP are optional.</small></div>
 </footer>
 <p class="de-note">Architecture references pinned to Agno <a href={'https://github.com/agno-agi/agno/tree/'+revision} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{revision.slice(0,8)}</a>. These are illustrative source-grounded diagrams, not inferred call stacks. <a href="/en/labs/agno-architecture-v2/">Return to Atlas V2 →</a></p>
</div>
